# Cline Rules: opensourcefeed.org /software/ Section

## Project Context

This is a Jekyll static site for opensourcefeed.org's `/software/` section. It covers individual software pages and open source alternatives. Built with Jekyll collections, Liquid templating, and mobile-first SASS.

## Tech Stack

- Jekyll 4.x (GitHub Pages compatible)
- Liquid templating
- SASS (via jekyll-sass-converter)
- No JavaScript frameworks
- No CSS frameworks (custom SASS only)

## Code Style Rules

### SASS
- Mobile-first: base styles target mobile, use `@include respond-to($breakpoint)` for larger screens
- Use variables from `_sass/_variables.scss` for colors, spacing, typography
- Use mixins from `_sass/_mixins.scss` for responsive patterns
- Never hardcode breakpoint values — use the `respond-to` mixin
- Keep partials focused: one concern per file
- Compressed output in production (set in `_config.yml`)

### Liquid
- Use `site.softwares | where: "slug", X | first` pattern for cross-referencing collections
- Never hardcode software descriptions in layouts — always pull from source `_softwares/` file
- Use `assign` tags to store looked-up objects before rendering
- 2-space indentation in Liquid templates

### HTML
- Semantic HTML5 elements (`article`, `section`, `nav`, `header`, `footer`)
- All images must have descriptive `alt` text
- All pages must have breadcrumbs
- All pages must have canonical URL in `<head>`

## Content Policy (Critical)

**Non-overlap is enforced structurally via layouts.** Never bypass this by adding content to the wrong page type:

- Software pages: feature breakdowns, use cases, platform support ONLY
- Alternatives pages: "why switch" content (2-3 sentences) ONLY
- Landing pages: auto-generated from front matter ONLY (no body content)

See `docs/CONTENT-POLICY.md` for the full matrix.

## File Conventions

- Collection files: `_softwares/[slug].md`, `_alternatives/[slug].md`
- Filenames must match `slug` front matter field
- Layouts: `_layouts/[name].html`
- Includes: `_includes/[name].html`
- SASS partials: `_sass/_[name].scss` (prefixed with underscore)
- Main stylesheet: `assets/css/main.scss` (imports all partials)

## Front Matter Requirements

Every collection file must have:
- `layout` — matches the layout file name
- `title` — page title (quoted)
- `slug` — matches filename
- `description` — 1-2 sentences for meta tags and cards
- `last_modified_at` — ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD)

Software pages additionally need: `type`, `license`, `website`, `platforms`, `category`, `tagline`

### Optional: `featured_image`

Software pages may optionally set `featured_image` to a filename only (e.g. `featured_image: qbittorrent.jpg`) — unlike `logo`, which stores a full relative path, the folder is fixed and assembled in Liquid. Files live in `assets/images/software-featured/`, standardized at 1200×630 (OG/Twitter card size), ~200KB max. When set, it renders as a hero image above the body content and takes priority over `logo` for `og:image`/`twitter:image`/JSON-LD `image`. Optional `featured_image_alt` overrides the default alt text (`page.title`). Pages without `featured_image` are unaffected — behavior falls back to `logo`/site default exactly as before.

## SEO Requirements

- Unique `<title>` and `<meta description>` on every page
- JSON-LD structured data on every page (type depends on page type)
- `dateModified` meta tag from `last_modified_at`
- Canonical URLs on every page
- Image alt text on all logos

## AdSense

- Use `{% include ad.html slot="position-name" %}` for ad placements
- Ads are config-driven (`site.adsense.enabled` and `site.adsense.client_id`)
- When disabled, placeholder divs show — do not remove these
- Ad positions: below header, mid-content (on content pages); below title, between sections (on landing pages)

## Testing Before Completion

Always run before marking task complete:
1. `bundle exec jekyll build` — must succeed with no errors
2. `bundle exec jekyll serve` — verify pages render
3. Check internal links work (no 404s)
4. Verify responsive at 320px, 768px, 1200px
5. Verify content non-overlap policy is maintained

## Do Not

- Do not add JavaScript frameworks (React, Vue, etc.)
- Do not add CSS frameworks (Bootstrap, Tailwind, etc.)
- Do not hardcode software data in layout files
- Do not duplicate content across page types
- Do not use marketing language — keep tone neutral and factual
- Do not remove ad placeholder slots
- Do not change permalink structures without updating all internal links